Z||000006||William Federle||08-26-2000||11:56 AM||||I think that after the torque converter locks up, the rpm should drop. I think on a recent post by theogre I read that you can test it by just tapping the brake slightly after you get up to a certain speed (40 or 50 MPH. You should see the RPM's increase momentarily when the torque convertor releases the clutch. <P>       If that's working, then I guess your rpm should depend on the final ratio of your transaxle. I think there's a web site (maybe the Fiero Online Service Guide) where you can determine your transaxle final ratio from the option codes on a sticker located on the inside of your front compartment. <P><p>[This message has been edited by William Federle (edited 08-26-2000).]||||reg||1
